# --- Pick ONE way to supply your Garmin Personal API key ---
# Create a key at https://connect.garmin.com/app/settings/personalApiToken
#
# IMPORTANT: do not paste the key into an interactive prompt. A prompt can
# truncate a long key silently; the result then fails with HTTP 401 and an empty
# body. Store it from the clipboard and verify the character count. See README.

# A. A command that prints the key (most secure: nothing in plaintext at rest).
#    Store it first, from the clipboard:
#      K=$(pbpaste | tr -d '\r\n'); security add-generic-password -a "$USER" \
#        -s garmin-personal-api -U -w "$K"; unset K
# GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_KEY_COMMAND="security find-generic-password -s garmin-personal-api -w"
#    1Password:  op read "op://Private/Garmin/credential"
#    pass:       pass show garmin/personal-api

# B. The key alone in ~/.config/garmin/connect-personal-api-key (chmod 600).
#    pbpaste | tr -d '\r\n' > ~/.config/garmin/connect-personal-api-key
#    Nothing to set here.

# C. The key itself. Simplest, least protected.
GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_KEY=

# --- Optional ---
# Defaults to https://personal.connectapi.garmin.com
# Use https://personal.connectapi.garmin.cn for Garmin China accounts.
# GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_BASE_URL=
